  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Alpheratz",
    "description": "Binary star in the constellation of Andromeda",
    "summary": "Alpheratz is a prominent star system in the constellation of Andromeda. Pronounced, it has the Bayer designation Alpha Andromedae, Latinised from α Andromedae, and abbreviated Alpha And or α And, respectively. Alpheratz is the brightest star in the constellation when Mirach undergoes its periodical dimming. Immediately northeast of the constellation of Pegasus, it is the upper left star of the Great Square of Pegasus. It is located at a distance of 97 light-years from Earth.",
